c211 record: {"id": "M3-c211", "lesson": "L08", "front": "In Section 3, what does orthogonalizing a shape against the earlier shapes mean?", "back": "Assuming F1 to F4 of Lesson 4 and at least three distinct tenor values, it means subtracting from the shape its orthogonal projection onto the span of the earlier shapes (Lesson 7, Theorem 1.2). Under that assumption the earlier shapes are linearly independent, which is the hypothesis of that theorem."}
